ranching source, auto mode hard deny rules, and hooks now expose effort level via effort.level and $CLAUDE_EFFORT environment variable.\",\n    33→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    34→    \"url\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\",\n    35→    \"date\": \"2026-05-04\",\n    36→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    37→  },\n    38→  {\n    39→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    40→    \"title\": \"Bugbot Effort Levels and PR Review enhancements\",\n    41→    \"description\": \"Teams admins and individual users can now customize Bugbot's effort level for PR reviews with three configurations: Default (optimized for speed), High (more reasoning, more expensive), or Custom (natural language instructions). Also introduced new PR review experience with inline review threads, commits tab, and changes tab with file tree navigation.\",\n    42→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    43→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    44→    \"date\": \"2026-05-11\",\n    45→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    46→  },\n    47→  {\n    48→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    49→    \"title\": \"v3.3: Cloud agent reliability fixes\",\n    50→    \"description\": \"Fixed various cloud agent timing and hydration edge cases that could degrade reliability.\",\n    51→    \"updateType\": \"bugfix\",\n    52→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    53→    \"date\": \"2026-05-06\",\n    54→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    55→  },\n    56→  {\n    57→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    58→    \"title\": \"Microsoft Teams integration\",\n    59→    \"description\": \"Cursor is now available in Microsoft Teams. Users can mention @Cursor in any Teams channel to delegate tasks to cloud agents or pull information from Cursor. It automatically picks the right repository and model based on prompt and recent agent activity.\",\n    60→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    61→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    62→    \"date\": \"2026-05-01\",\n    63→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    64→  },\n    65→  {\n    66→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    67→    \"title\": \"PR Review, Build Plan in Parallel, and Split PRs\",\n    68→    \"description\": \"New PR review experience with Reviews tab showing inline threads and top-level comments, Commits tab for focused history, and Changes tab with file tree. Can now execute on plans faster by multitasking across tasks with 'Build in Parallel' feature, and split changes into PRs using quick action that identifies logical slices.\",\n    69→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    70→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n    71→    \"date\": \"2026-04-27\",\n    72→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    73→  }\n    74→]\n    75→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
