er the keyboard.\n                        </div>\n                        <span class=\"insight-source\">Podcast</span>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/08/how-anthropics-mythos-firefox-cybersecurity/\" target=\"_blank\">How Anthropic's Mythos has rewritten Firefox's approach to cybersecurity</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-author\">Russell Brandom</div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                            TechCrunch covers how Mozilla used Claude Mythos to dramatically scale up vulnerability discovery in Firefox, going from 20-30 bugs per month to 423 in April.\n                        </div>\n                        <span class=\"insight-source\">TechCrunch</span>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40811876\" target=\"_blank\">An AI coding agent needs to reduce your maintenance costs</a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-author\">jamesshore.com</div>\n                        <div class=\"insight-description\">\n                            James Shore explores the economic reality of AI coding agents - they should reduce maintenance costs, not just initial development time.\n                        </div>\n                        <span class=\"insight-source\">HN</span>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"insight-item\">\n                        <div class=\"insight-title\">\n                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/10/nyt-ai-hallucination-correction/\" target=\"_blank\">New York Times AI Hallucination Correction</a>\n                  